% You are an expert Python engineer. Write `pdd/local_work_items.py`.

<include>context/python_preamble.prompt</include>

% Role & Scope
  Provide the local, filesystem-backed work item that stands in for a GitHub
  issue across PDD's agentic workflows. A GitHub issue played three roles at
  once — the request the workflow implements, the store for resumable
  multi-step state, and the channel a human uses to steer a run mid-flight —
  and this module must satisfy all three from disk alone. It MUST NOT invoke
  `gh`, open a network connection, or import any other `pdd` module.

% Non-responsibilities
  Routing a CLI argument to a workflow, deciding when a workflow runs, and
  rendering work items for the terminal all belong to `pdd/commands/work.py`
  and the orchestrators. This module only stores and projects data.

<contract_rules>
R1 - Reference syntax
`parse_local_ref` MUST accept `local:N`, `local#N`, `local/N`, `work:N`,
`work-item:N`, and `workitem:N`, case-insensitively and tolerating surrounding
whitespace, returning the positive integer N. It MUST return None for a GitHub
URL, a prompt filename, a non-string, a missing number, and any N <= 0, so a
routing predicate can use it without misclassifying an ordinary argument.

R2 - Routing discriminator
A local work item MUST be addressable as the triple
(`LOCAL_OWNER`, <project name>, <number>), because every deep call site in the
agentic layer already receives repo_owner/repo_name/issue_number. `is_local_owner`
is the discriminator those call sites branch on. This module MUST NOT require a
process-global "local mode" flag to answer that question.

R3 - Storage layout and durability
Work items live under `<project_root>/.pdd/work_items/`, one JSON file per item
(`item_<n>.json`) plus an `index.json` holding the allocators. Every write MUST
be atomic (write to a temporary file, then rename) so an interrupted run cannot
leave a half-written item. A read error MUST raise `LocalWorkItemError` naming
the path rather than returning a silently empty item.

R4 - Monotonic comment ids
Comment ids MUST be allocated from a persisted counter and MUST NEVER be reused,
including after a comment is deleted. Mid-run steering drains comments whose id
exceeds a stored cursor, so a reused id would silently replay an already-drained
instruction. The index MUST also record which work item owns each comment id,
because the state helpers address comments by id alone.

R5 - Shape compatibility
`github_shaped_issue` MUST emit every field existing callers read off a
`gh api .../issues/N` payload: `number`, `title`, `body`, `state`,
`labels` as `[{"name": ...}]`, `user.login`, `comments_url`, `comments`,
`created_at`, `updated_at`. `github_shaped_comment` MUST emit `id`,
`user.login`, `body`, `created_at`, `updated_at`. Timestamps MUST use GitHub's
ISO-8601 `Z` form so the existing timestamp parsers accept them unchanged.

R6 - `since` filtering matches GitHub
`list_comments` MUST return only comments whose activity timestamp (updated_at,
falling back to created_at) is strictly after `since`, mirroring the GitHub API
parameter. It MUST return None — not an empty list — when the work item does
not exist, so callers can distinguish "no such item" from "no comments".

R7 - gh-shaped request service
`serve_gh_api` MUST answer `repos/local/<repo>/issues/<n>`,
`repos/local/<repo>/issues/<n>/comments`, and the sentinel
`pdd-local://work-items/<n>/comments` with the JSON text `gh` would have
printed, and MUST return None for any other path so a caller falls through to
the real `gh` unchanged.

R8 - Local-only guard
`local_only_enabled` MUST report whether `PDD_LOCAL_ONLY` is set to a truthy
value. When it is, the agentic layer reports the `gh` binary as absent, so
every GitHub helper takes its existing "no gh" branch. This function MUST NOT
itself perform that suppression.

R9 - State validity
`update_work_item` MUST reject any state other than `open` or `closed`, MUST
refresh `updated_at` only when something actually changed, and MUST return None
for a missing item rather than creating one.
</contract_rules>

% Deliverables
- Code: `pdd/local_work_items.py`
